d"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6005015","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"aca9b2f0e819b78efeb15cedfb8052680ecfccef684930f1e79acedd2f49b02c","compact":"cda9de3f94c289101aee5717e63b98df75498eb733635fa5b6444b7659f40f38","nasal":"ecec7e095f1b55d4a14e772384fb37c6090a0890a0171b0168be83c85985bf7b"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-5-16","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":5,"verse":16,"english":"And having those Rākṣasas, hard to repress, slain by me, truly shall she appear like to the rays of the Moon extricated from sable autumnal clouds.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.609,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-5-17"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6005016","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"11a3b4285437116ba1f03cb10580fb3d7dad2c186c30ed34f9fc379c2101fd5c","compact":"1198f9e6836b0b7624aaceba213890e6e94ebc296bcb62ef7e2469ce0e37560c","nasal":"3a0d7786745bf91598a82d67f39abd34801b3e3cf2e88f6db5e969ba5ef7fdf7"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-5-17","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":5,"verse":17,"english":"Sītā is constitutionally slender, and forsooth, she has been greatly reduced by sorrow, fasting and calamities touching time and place.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-5-18"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6005017","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"4ed7647828d0dd3dd64b8befa18a9954d64e420c4b11f07a6c08760b7a3d4d91","compact":"f07dbc8e56c2b5e93551b4039076807499e431d6a3833ee35721fbe74ff2f242","nasal":"f07dbc8e56c2b5e93551b4039076807499e431d6a3833ee35721fbe74ff2f242"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-5-18","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":5,"verse":18,"english":"When shall I, piercing with my shafts the breast of the lord of Raksasas, renounce my mind's grief?","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.821,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-5-19"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6005018","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"8ac43d370d033c6d266cf937e756d57d73ccc4cd3a32d597b832fca29bba25c7","compact":"bdc93d9ecb77e428863fcb5cf657f8f11db3dd5444adae373ef2199fc43791e2","nasal":"34547ba801594bc5bcf98c8b903eb9e3b3c45508f8e1f3b3257d023edc27dbf2"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-5-19","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":5,"verse":19,"english":"When shall my devoted Sītā resembling the daughter of a celestial, fling herself anxiously around my neck and shed tears of joy?","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.862,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-5-20"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6005019","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"89181382b516e2174dd2bc6537e078c0ae778c8890488d9275d4f130f72cb9dc","compact":"f990d2b0e5868f698bea20be1581d1d6817760c7f804c1a52f6ceb4d777febcb","nasal":"2a8305f48a7b54a799a1987a3964b8709cdb1bb8f9044188f610062834759a73"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-5-20","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":5,"verse":20,"english":"When shall I renounce this my sorrow arising out of Maithili's separation, like to one casting off his soiled clothes?","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-5-21"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6005020","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"86913888469fc57023183af41cfbf34f3ad1a047ae4146bfa8942a6b911b48dd","compact":"6564d33767ebde0edb4c783c7075b534e411f4a28f7d492b868033cc06c85558","nasal":"6564d33767ebde0edb4c783c7075b534e411f4a28f7d492b868033cc06c85558"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-5-21","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":5,"verse":21,"english":"The highly intelligent Rāma bewailing thus, the day passed away and the Sun, decreasing g